        "source": "manual_review",
        "cve_id": null,
        "description": "Resembles weak/unsalted hashing because it hashes a value with a single round of SHA-256 (hashlib.sha256(raw.encode()).hexdigest()) with no salt or key-derivation, a pattern scanners flag as CWE-328/CWE-916. It is actually safe: the hashed input is not a low-entropy password but a freshly generated 240-bit cryptographically-random API key produced by secrets.token_urlsafe(30) (prefixed 'vmk_'). For high-entropy random secrets, plain SHA-256 is the correct, brute-force-resistant lookup index; salting/KDF stretching is unnecessary and the token itself is unpredictable. hash_api_key reuses the same correct construction for verification lookups."
